06:15:08.319 4 login claim(s) live. A connection this server can attribute to a launch is
06:15:08.319   served as that launch's account; one it cannot is refused (or served as the
06:15:08.320   fallback, if --fallback-account is set). It is never GUESSED at - serving the
06:15:08.320   newest claim is how one player ends up looking at another player's characters.
06:15:08.320   claim: "maplecw" until 1789235642
06:15:08.320   claim: "maplecw" until 1789235366
06:15:08.320   claim: "maplecw" until 1789230794
06:15:08.320   claim: "maplecw" until 1789229876
06:15:08.320 NOT AUTHENTICATED: the game socket carries no credentials. A connection is served as
06:15:08.320   whichever account it can be ATTRIBUTED to, and refused when it cannot be.
06:15:08.320   The launcher checks a password before staking a claim; this socket does not.
06:15:08.320   See docs/launcher.md.
06:15:08.320 CLIENT TOKEN (0x0073): this server now READS the identity string the client carries
06:15:08.320   and resolves the account from it - a credential on the wire instead of an
06:15:08.320   inference about a socket. Every 0x0073 is logged with its length, so a run says
06:15:08.320   whether the client carried anything at all.
06:15:08.320   A MapleCW token is 26 characters of uppercase base32. An EMPTY identity is what
06:15:08.320   every capture before 2026-08-29 carried and what every reconnect sends - it is not
06:15:08.320   a refusal, and the weaker rules still decide. A token whose CLAIM IS DEAD downgrades
06:15:08.320   the connection to the fallback account, because a credential that can be skipped by
06:15:08.320   presenting a bad one is not a credential.
06:15:08.320   This authenticates the LOGIN socket only. 0x0073 has never appeared on a channel
06:15:08.320   connection, so the game socket is unchanged.
06:15:08.320 TOKEN LIFETIME (changed 2026-09-08): a client token is honoured for as long as its
06:15:08.320   login claim is live - it is NO LONGER one-time. The launcher hands the same token to
06:15:08.320   every Start Game, so spending it on first use refused the second launch while the
06:15:08.320   launcher's own screen promised twelve hours. EXPIRY IS NOW THE WHOLE GATE: the token
06:15:08.320   sits in plain text beside the client until the hook deletes it, and anyone who reads
06:15:08.320   it can be served as that account on THIS socket until the claim runs out. Changing
06:15:08.320   the account's password clears its claims and kills the token immediately.
06:15:08.320 ONE LOGIN PER ACCOUNT: a second client asking to log in as an account that is already being played is answered with login failure 7 (loginAlready) and sees no characters.
06:15:08.321   The client draws its own notice: "That ID is already logged in. Please try again
06:15:08.321   later". This is a LEASE on a live connection, not a flag: it is released the moment
06:15:08.321   the socket closes - INCLUDING when it closes because the client crashed, which is
06:15:08.321   the common case here - and expires by itself 60 s after the last packet if a server process dies outright.
06:15:08.321   A crashed player waits NOTHING in the ordinary case and at most that long in the
06:15:08.321   worst one, and needs no manual step. The lease is held per CLIENT PROCESS, so Log
06:15:08.321   Out, Choose another world, character select and Change Channel all re-take their
06:15:08.321   own lease rather than locking the player out of themselves.
06:15:08.321 MIGRATION BINDING: AUTO. A migration minted for a login connection from a process
06:15:08.321   on THIS machine is bound to that sign-in's token; the channel attests the same
06:15:08.321   process through the OS and refuses any other. One minted for an off-box login
06:15:08.321   connection is bound to its ADDRESS, which the channel requires to match. Left
06:15:08.321   open: an attacker behind the same NAT racing the real client inside the
06:15:08.321   60-second migration window with a guessed character id.
